\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I think, when I read that sweet story of old,
\par When Jesus was here among men,
\par How He called little children as lambs to His fold,
\par I should like to have been with them then;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I wish that His hands had been placed on my head
\par That his arms had been thrown around me,
\par And that I might have seen His kind look when He said:
\par Let the little ones come unto me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Yet still to His footstool in prayer I may go,
\par And ask for a share in His love;
\par And if I now earnestly seek Him below,
\par I shall shall see Him and hear Him above,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In that beautiful place He is gone to prepare
\par For all who are washed and forgiven;
\par And many dear children are gathering there,
\par For of such is the kingom of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But thousands and thousands who wander and fall
\par Never heard of that heavenly home;
\par I should like them to know there is a room for them all.
\par And that Jesus has bid them to come.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I long for the joy of that glorious time,
\par The sweetest and brightest and best,
\par When the dear little children of every clime
\par Shall crowd to His arms and be blessed.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

